  "reasoning": "Scientific consensus confirmed by marine biology sources establishes that octopuses possess three hearts and blue blood. Two branchial hearts pump blood through the gills to collect oxygen, while a single systemic heart circulates blood through the rest of the body. Their blood is blue because it relies on hemocyanin, a copper-based oxygen-transport protein that is particularly efficient in cold, low-oxygen aquatic environments.",
